<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $313.3 mln May 28.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $313.3 mln May 28.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $313.3 million deficit on May 28 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 28</p>
<p>Exports: $271.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $340.5 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $297.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $542.4 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $313.3 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.933 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $5.155 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $7.251 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $5.382 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.647 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
